<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Central Bank lowers special T-bill rate.</title>
<headline>Philippine Central Bank lowers special T-bill rate.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank said on Tuesday it lowered borrowing rates on its special series Treasury bills.</p>
<p>Its 85-day T-bill now fetches a rate of 10.63 percent from a previous 10.65; and the 141-day bill, 10.95 from 11.00 percent.</p>
<p>Dealers said the Central Bank's move signalled it did not want rates to move up after Monday's primary auction of Treasury bills yielded slightly higher rates.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
